  "body": "## What changed\n\nEvery Tormach PathPilot mill tool change posted `G53 G0 Z0`, `G30`, `T.. M6`, `G43 H..`, `S.. M3`, then `G0 X.. Y..` with no Z lift between. A bare `G30` leaves Z at the stored G30 height. One stored below the part top (the user's PathPilot Hub sim had machine Z -1.5611, the same cause as #1594) rapids the tool sideways at that height into the part or the vise. M3's review of #1600 raised this to P1.\n\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps` `startPreamble`: `liftZ()` (`G53 G0 Z0`, or the machine's stated safe Z, #495) right after `G43 H..`. It comes before the spindle start and before the section's first X/Y or A move, including the program's first tool change. The tool-change `G30` stays (PathPilot's convention).\n- 4th axis: the new lift comes before `G0 A..`. The index's own lift is kept, so an indexed section has a second, harmless `G53 G0 Z0` just before `G0 A`.\n- The issue's other two bare G30s are kept, with the reasons in `docs/decisions/1596-toolchange-lift.md`:\n  - **Plasma.** The G30 height is PathPilot plasma's traverse height (rapids carry no Z, and M205 returns to it).\n  - **Lathe.** G30 is the X/Z safe spot and there is no \"up\" to lift to. The lathe's diagonal approach from G30 is a different hazard, filed as #1604 (P3).\n- Not stacked: #1600 merged first, and this branch is one commit on current main.\n\n## Pins and mutations\n\nNew `crates/app/tests/tormach_toolchange_lift.rs`:\n\n| Pin | Proves |\n|---|---|\n| `every_tormach_mill_tool_change_lifts_z_before_moving_xy` | Every shipped Tormach mill, both tool changes (the first included): `G43` is followed by `G53 G0 Z0`, the G30 is kept, and there is a lift between each G30 and the next X/Y move. |\n| `a_stated_safe_z_is_the_lift_after_the_tool_change` | `safe_retract` 2.0 gives `G53 G0 Z2` after each `G43`. |\n| `a_fourth_axis_section_lifts_z_before_the_a_index` | microARC 4: the lift after `G43` comes before `G0 A90`, and A is the first sideways move. |\n\nMutation check against `tormach.cps`: each mutation was applied, the pins run, and the file restored. All pins were green again after the restore.\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Remove the lift | 3/3 pins red |\n| Hard-code the lift to `Z0` | `a_stated_safe_z…` red |\n| Move the lift to the end of the preamble (after the spindle and coolant) | 3/3 red |\n\n`tormach_program_end` (#1600) stayed green under every mutation and on the fix: the program end is unchanged.\n\nUpdated tests:\n- `tormach_safe_retract::a_stated_safe_z_posts_that_z`: the `G53 G0 Z<stated>` count goes from 3 to 5.\n- `probe_spindle_stop` (post crate): a `G53` line is a machine-coordinate retract, not the section's first move. The probe `M5` still comes before any work move.\n\n## Goldens\n\nRegenerated with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1`. The tester-kit `.camproj` rewrite that came with it was reverted (unrelated version/float noise).\n\n- 33 `.nc` files changed: 24 app goldens (tormach + inch/tormach + synth_tormach), 8 post goldens (recorded tormach + ream) and the microARC tester-kit `.nc`.\n- `git diff -U0 -- '*.nc'` shows exactly **35 added lines, all `G53 G0 Z0`, and 0 removed**: one per tool change.\n- No lathe or plasma goldens changed. No snapshot PNGs were touched.\n\n## Gates (macOS, debug)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: ok. The post suites passed (15 s). The app suites passed: the whole app set, since shared goldens changed (800 s).\n- Also run: post `recorded_streams` / `script_tormach_plasma`, and app `recorded_post_streams` / `posting` / `lathe_post_tormach` / `tormach_lathes`. All ok.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No PathPilot Hub or machine run of the new tool change.\n- Windows arms of per-OS readings were not run.\n\nChangelog: Tormach mill posts lift Z straight up (`G53 G0 Z<safe>`) after every tool change, before the first X/Y or A move, so a low stored G30 never carries the tool sideways into the part (posted output changes: one line per tool change) (#1596)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1596\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
